I implemented backend/app/ml/cnn_model.py exactly per your spec and added the required dependencies (tensorflow, scikit-learn) to backend/requirements.txt. Below is a simple, line‑by‑line explanation of what each part does, and how the logic matches the requirements.

File: backend/app/ml/cnn_model.py — simple, detailed explanation
Imports
dataclass, Path, Any: used for clean structured return types and file paths.
numpy: for numeric arrays and vectorized operations.
sklearn.metrics: for precision, recall, F1, AUC, and confusion matrix.
tensorflow.keras: for the CNN layers, model, training callbacks, and optimizer.
PredictionResult dataclass
This is the output of predict_single. It contains:

afib_probability: number from 0–1.
prediction: "AFIB" or "NORMAL".
confidence: distance from 0.5.
uncertain: True if probability is in the 0.35–0.65 range.
class AFibCNN
Encapsulates the CNN model and all operations.

__init__
Starts with self.model = None so we can build lazily.

build(input_shape)
Creates and compiles the CNN.

Architecture exactly as in your diagram:

Input (window_samples, 1)
Conv1D(32, kernel=50, relu)
Conv1D(32, kernel=25, relu)
Conv1D(64, kernel=10, relu)
Conv1D(64, kernel=5, relu)
GlobalAveragePooling1D
Dense(64, relu)
Dropout(0.3)
Dense(1, sigmoid)
Compile:

binary_crossentropy loss
Adam optimizer
metrics: accuracy, precision, recall, AUC
train(...)
Trains the model with proper callbacks:

EarlyStopping on val_auc, patience=10
ReduceLROnPlateau, factor=0.5, patience=5
optional ModelCheckpoint (saves best weights)
Returns the training history.

evaluate(X_test, y_test)
Runs predict to get probabilities.
Converts to class labels using 0.5 threshold.
Calculates:
accuracy
precision
recall
F1
AUC
confusion matrix
Finds uncertain predictions in 0.35–0.65 range.
Counts false negatives (critical for medical).
Returns all of these in a dict.

predict(X)
Ensures model is built.
Ensures input is shape (N, window_samples, 1).
Returns probabilities as a flat array (N,).
predict_single(segment)
Wraps a single segment into batch form.
Returns PredictionResult with probability, label, confidence, uncertain flag.
save(path) / load(path, input_shape)
Save and load weights only.
load rebuilds first to match shape.
load_ecg_weights_for_ppg(...)
Implements transfer learning:

Builds model with new input shape.
Loads ECG weights.
Freezes all Conv1D layers.
Recompiles with smaller learning rate (1e-4) for fine‑tuning.
_ensure_model, _ensure_built, _ensure_3d
Safety helpers:

_ensure_model: fail fast if model isn’t built.
_ensure_built: build lazily using data shape.
_ensure_3d: ensures (N, window_samples, 1) input format.
