signalApi.ts — simple, line‑by‑line explanation
import axios from "axios";
Brings in Axios for HTTP requests.

import type { CardiacResult } from "../types";
Reuses the shared type for cardiac responses.

import { API_BASE_URL } from "../utils/constants";
Base URL for the backend, so you don’t hardcode it.

const api = axios.create({ baseURL: API_BASE_URL });
Creates a reusable Axios instance with the base URL.

getRecords()
api.get("/api/cardiac/records")
Calls the backend to get a list of available record IDs.
Returns the array of strings.
uploadPPG(file)
Creates FormData and appends the file under "file".
POST /api/cardiac/upload with multipart form data.
Returns CardiacResult.
loadMITBIH(recordId)
POST /api/cardiac/mitbih/{recordId}
Returns CardiacResult.
loadMIMIC(recordId)
POST /api/cardiac/mimic/{recordId}
Returns CardiacResult.
simulatePPG(scenario)
POST /api/cardiac/simulate with { scenario } in JSON body.
Returns CardiacResult.
neurologicalApi.ts — simple, line‑by‑line explanation
import axios from "axios";
Axios is used for HTTP requests.

import { API_BASE_URL } from "../utils/constants";
Base URL for the backend.

const api = axios.create({ baseURL: API_BASE_URL });
Creates a reusable Axios instance.

analyzeFace(imageFile)
Creates FormData.
Adds the image file as "file".
POSTs to /api/neurological/face/analyze.
Returns response.data.
analyzeFaceSession(images)
Creates FormData.
Adds each image file as "files".
POSTs to /api/neurological/face/session.
Returns response.data.
addFaceBaseline(imageFile)
Same pattern as analyzeFace, but POSTs to /face/baseline.
analyzeVoice(audioFile)
Same pattern, POSTs to /voice/analyze.
addVoiceBaseline(audioFile)
Same pattern, POSTs to /voice/baseline.
runSpeechTest(promptIndex, audioFile)
Adds prompt_index and file to FormData.
POSTs to /voice/speech-test.
Returns response.data.
getBaselineStatus()
GET /api/neurological/baseline/status.
Returns response.data.

