App.tsx (simple line‑by‑line)

import { BrowserRouter, Route, Routes, useLocation } ... brings in React Router so we can define pages and track the current URL.
import { AnimatePresence, motion } ... enables animated page transitions.
import "./App.css"; loads layout styling for the app shell.
import Sidebar ... Navbar ... brings in the layout components.
import ...Page lines load each page component.
function AnimatedRoutes() defines a helper that handles route animations.
const location = useLocation(); reads the current URL so transitions happen on route change.
<AnimatePresence mode="wait"> ensures the outgoing page animates out before the new one animates in.
<motion.div ...> wraps the route content with a fade/slide animation.
key={location.pathname} makes each URL a distinct animation state.
initial/animate/exit/transition define the simple fade + slide behavior.
<Routes location={location}> tells Router to use the tracked location for transitions.
<Route path="/" ...> sets Dashboard as the home page.
<Route path="/cardiac" ...> sets the Cardiac page route.
<Route path="/neurological" ...> sets the Neurological page route.
<Route path="/neuro-tests" ...> sets the Neuro Tests page route.
<Route path="/demo" ...> sets the Demo page route.
function App() defines the root component.
<BrowserRouter> enables SPA routing.
<div className="app-shell"> is the main layout container (sidebar + main area).
<Sidebar /> renders the left nav (always visible on desktop).
<div className="app-main"> holds the top navbar and current page.
<Navbar /> renders the top bar.
<AnimatedRoutes /> renders the current page with transitions.
export default App makes the component available to main.tsx.
main.tsx (simple line‑by‑line)

import { StrictMode } ... enables React’s strict checks in dev.
import { createRoot } ... creates the React 18/19 root.
import { Provider } ... connects Redux to React.
import { ThemeProvider } ... enables the MUI theme.
import "./index.css"; loads global styles and CSS variables.
import App from "./App"; brings in the main app UI.
import { store } ... loads the Redux store.
import { appTheme } ... loads the MUI theme we created.
createRoot(...).render(...) attaches React to the DOM.
<StrictMode> wraps the app for dev checks.
<Provider store={store}> makes Redux state available to all components.
<ThemeProvider theme={appTheme}> applies the MUI theme globally.
<App /> renders the app itself.
theme.ts (simple line‑by‑line)

import { createTheme } ... brings in MUI’s theme builder.
export const appTheme = createTheme({ ... }) creates and exports your theme.
palette sets brand colors to match your CSS variables.
typography sets default fonts, with display headings in Syne.
shape sets a consistent rounded corner radius.
App.css (simple line‑by‑line summary)

.app-shell creates a full‑height flex layout.
.app-main makes the right side a vertical stack (Navbar + page).
.route-wrapper adds padding around each page and lets it expand.
@media (max-width: 900px) stacks layout vertically on mobile.
